 compatibility means that any operational differences are invisible to people and programs alike.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="36322">compatibility</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533187">utangamanifu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10190_122191_1399228"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A command button used in a toolbar (or status bar).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="122191">toolbar button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399228">kitufe cha mwambaa zana</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10206_718_2118827"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any technology used to protect the interests of owners of digital content and services (such as copyright owners). Typically, authorized recipients or users must acquire a license in order to use the content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="718">digital rights management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118827">usimamiaji haki za tarakimu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10206_719_2118827"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any technology used to protect the interests of owners of digital content and services (such as copyright owners). Typically, authorized recipients or users must acquire a license in order to use the content.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="719">DRM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118827">usimamiaji haki za tarakimu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10208_413716_1918533"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A cell range that you consolidate in the destination area you specify.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="413716">source area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918533">eneo la chanzo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10218_358371_534875"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A database object that prints information formatted and organized according to your specifications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="358371">report</term><termNote type