al on phone and pretending to be another employee of company with a computer-related question.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="493916">social engineering</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2576732">uhandisi wa kijamii</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15139_362562_1952765"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type consisting of a 32-bit unsigned integer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="362562">DWORD</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1952765">DWORD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15139_48746_1952765"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A data type consisting of a 32-bit unsigned integer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="48746">dword</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1952765">DWORD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15140_320449_534725"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The € character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="320449">euro symbol</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534725">alama uro €</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15140_320450_534725"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The € character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="320450">EURO SIGN</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534725">alama uro €</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15144_346594_534823"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The time for which a dry or alkaline cell is able to produce an electric current before it needs to be replaced.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="346594">battery life</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534823">maisha ya betri</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15151_68314_533424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Characterized by conversational exchange of input and output, as when a user enters a question or command and the system immediately responds. The interactivity of microcomputers is one of the features that makes them approachable and easy to use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="68314">interactive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533424">ingiliani</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15153_304427_1389091"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An exponentiation operator used in some programming languages. For example, the expression 3^2 represents the number 3 raised to the second power.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="304427">caret</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1389091">kareti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15154_2421378_1545864"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A work item that records a possible event with an undesirable outcome.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2421378">risk event</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></lan