ces. The minimum quantity that qualifies as a bulk order is set by individual companies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="178508">bulk order</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2344313">agizo kubwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15386_154964_533984"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A delay of the amount of time that elapses before a character begins repeating when you hold down a key.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="154964">repeat delay</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533984">kawizo la uradidi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15396_148352_1389389"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">E-mail accounts and folders that you can group and set common options for, such as whether to download headers or messages, size limits on downloaded messages, behavior online vs. offline, and time interval for connecting to the server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="148352">Send/Receive group</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1389389">kikundi cha kutuma/kupokea</term><termNote typ