pe that provides a view of the surface chart from above, with colors representing specific ranges of values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592355">contour chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918571">chati ya kontua</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16507_592356_1918572"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A contour chart displayed without color.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592356">wireframe contour chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918572">chati contua ya fremuwaya</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16508_2909978_1918573"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that displays data in rings, where each ring represents a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2909978">donut</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918573">chati ya miduara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16508_592357_1918573"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart that displays data in rings, where each ring represents a data series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592357">doughnut chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918573">chati ya miduara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16511_592360_1918574"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A doughnut chart that displays the contribution of each value to a total while emphasizing individual values, by showing each slice of the doughnut as "pulled out," or separate, from the whole.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592360">exploded doughnut chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918574">chati ya mduara lipuo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16513_592362_1918575"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A best-fit curved trendline that is used when the rate of change in the data increases or decreases quickly and then levels out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592362">logarithmic trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918575">mstari wa mwelekeo wa logarithimu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16514_592363_1918576"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used when data fluctuates.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592363">polynomial trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918576">msitari mwelekeo ya majina mengi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16516_592365_1918577"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used with data sets that compare measurements that increase at a specific rate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="592365">power trendline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918577">mstari wa mwelekeo wa nguvu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16518_592368_1918578"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A curved trendline that is used when da