 feature of Remote Desktop Services that enables the user to access a program remotely through Remote Desktop Services but have it appear as if it is running on the user's local computer. Users can run RemoteApp programs side by side with their local programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616468">Terminal Services RemoteApp</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1750686">RemoteApp</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="16775_616469_1750686"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Remote Desktop Services that enables the user to access a program remotely through Remote Desktop Services but have it appear as if it is running on the user's local computer. Users can run RemoteApp programs side by side with their local programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616469">TS RemoteApp</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1750686">RemoteApp</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1679_1370400_1399305"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The W3C standard language used for writing XML schema documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1370400">XSD</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNot