oups. Typically, ribbon tabs are labeled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1309629">ribbon tab</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918814">kichupo cha riboni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1975_73133_533454"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A designation used to conduct sorting or searching operations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73133">keyword</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533454">neno msingi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19767_674770_2772223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A rating unit, e.g. assigning a "one-star rating" to an image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="674770">star</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2772223">nyota</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1978_45320_533257"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To enter numbers on a device, such as telephone or mobile, in order to make a phone call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="45320">dial</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533257">piga simu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19780_2466458_2469232"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The audio effect ​that creates the perception that there are many more sources of sound then are currently present. This is a well-known and industry term for the technique of creating a surround sound experience for users listening to audio with regular stereo headphones.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2466458">virtual surround sound</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2469232">sauti pepe ya mzunguko</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19780_682693_2469232"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The audio effect ​that creates the perception that there are many more sources of sound then are currently present. This is a well-known and industry term for the technique of creating a surround sound experience for users listening to audio with regular stereo headphones.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="682693">virtual surround</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2469232">sauti pepe ya mzunguko</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1979_63495_533395"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphic symbol used on the user interface to assist with navigation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="63495">icon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533395">ikoni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19792_685384_1918639"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An effect that applies to the exterior border around each character of your text or shape.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="685384">outline effect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918639">athari ya ufupisho</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19793_685388_1389173"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An effect that applies to th