/termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534871">kiungo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3633_44143_1396877"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In some dialog boxes, the command button that is selected or highlighted when the dialog box is initially displayed. The default button has a bold border, indicating that it will be chosen automatically if you press ENTER. You can override a default button by clicking Cancel or another command button.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44143">default button</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1396877">kitufe cha chaguo-msingi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3634_27320_533110"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To revoke an action by quitting it without saving any changes that it would result in.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27320">cancel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533110">katisha</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3638_53737_533336"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area in a window or record that stores a single data value.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="53737">field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533336">uga</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3643_323598_1396838"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tool in Windows Vista that backs up the entire computer (OS, settings, and files).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="323598">Complete PC Backup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1396838">Chelezo Complete PC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3644_116003_1399188"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A statistical measure of the amount by which a set of values differs from the arithmetical mean, equal to the square root of the mean of the differences' squares.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116003">standard deviation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399188">mkengeuko wastani</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3655_85228_533549"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hyphen that is used to prevent a hyphenated word, number, or phrase from breaking if it falls at the end of a line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85228">nonbreaking hyphen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533549">kistari fungamanishi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3657_16207_1951749"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A characteristic of an object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="16207">attribute</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1951749">sifa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3659_319140_1397134"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ( character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="319140">opening parenthesis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1397134">mabano funguzi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3662_77222_533492"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that makes the screen more readable by people who have low vision by creating a separate window that displays a magnified portion of the screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="77222">Magnifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533492">Kikuzi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36774_2070563_2119000"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A subset of settings and features that can be assigned to one of four slots in action center for quick, one-tap access. In addition, they can provide useful, actionable, or critical info regarding the setting or feature.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2070563">quick action</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119000">hatua ya haraka</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36775_2070564_2119106"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An app that is built using the Windows universal app platform. Developers can create a Windows universal app that runs on all Windows-based device types, or they can choose to limit an app to specific devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2070564">universal app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119106">programu inayotumika kwa kila kifaa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36775_2247950_2119106"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An app that is built using the Windows universal app platform. Developers can create a Windows universal app that runs on all Windows-based device types, or they can choose to limit an app to specific devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2247950">Windows universal app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119106">programu inayotumika kwa kila kifaa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36776_2070565_2118846"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To provide Wi-Fi credentials to Outlook.com contacts, Skype contacts, and Facebook friends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2070565">exchange</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118846">badilisha</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36778_2071066_2118894"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The phone's volume mode when in a call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071066">In-Call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118894">Simu ya Kuingia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36779_2071067_2118821"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The use of data connection in a roaming area. Generally making phone calls or using your data connection when the phone is roaming is more expensive, and the user will be charged additional fees for voice roaming calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071067">data roaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118821">kuzurura kwa data</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36780_2071068_2119129"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The connection on your phone that allows you to make phone calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071068">voice connection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119129">muunganisho wa sauti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36781_2071069_2119132"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A phone call made in a roaming area. Generally making phone calls or using your data connection when the phone is roaming is more expensive, and the user will be charged additional fees for voice roaming calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071069">voice roaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119132">kuzurura kwa sauti</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36783_2071243_2119022"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The setting that determines if the screen will rotate automatically when the phone is rotated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071243">screen rotation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119022">mzunguko wa skrini</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36784_2071244_2123484"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft operating system designed for handheld portable devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071244">Windows Embedded Handheld</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2123484">Windows Embedded Handheld</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36785_2071245_2123483"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft operating system built on Windows Phone 8 designed for handheld portable devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071245">Windows Embedded 8 Handheld</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2123483">Windows Embedded 8 Handheld</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36786_2071246_2119082"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A predetermined text reply that can be automatically sent in response to incoming calls, text messages, or both when Driving Mode is turned on. The text reply is sent with no action on the part of the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071246">text reply</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119082">majibu ya matini</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36787_2071247_2119083"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A response to an incoming call using a text message when the caller is a contact calling from a mobile phone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071247">text reply</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119083">majibu ya matini</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36791_2071377_2119059"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A photo you can choose to use as the background for some Live Tiles on the Start screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071377">Start background</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119059">Anza mandharinyuma</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36792_2071378_2119124"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows Phone feature to upgrade a phone call into a Skype video call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071378">video upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119124">badilisha kuwa video</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36793_2071379_2119142"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual setting that enables app screen content to display in a window.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071379">windowed mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2119142">modi ya dirisha</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36794_2071380_2118847"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual setting that is similar to “stretch” - the resolution of the phone screen is refitted to fill as much of the external screen as possible without compromising its dimensionality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071380">expanded screen mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118847">modi iliyopanuliwa ya skrini</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36795_2071381_2118993"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows desktop application that is required to enable users to project their phone screen to a Windows device using a USB connection.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071381">Project My Screen App</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118993">Kunyoosha Programu Yangu ya Skrini</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36805_2072311_2085517"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that unifies components across applications, such as people, conversations, calendars, emails, and files, to create a seamless collaboration experience. Creating a group anywhere in Microsoft 365 will automatically provision a corresponding Yammer conversation feed, an Outlook inbox and calendar, and a SharePoint document library for every Group member. Groups make these components persistent across applications, so that changes made to components in part of Microsoft 365 will carry through to the others, thus enabling a unified experience.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072311">Groups</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></