p that can be used to play and record movies and TV shows.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2254379">Movies &amp; TV</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2258232">Filamu na Televisheni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38707_2254408_2257415"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The community forum for Windows Insiders.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2254408">Windows Insider Community Forum</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2257415">Mkutano wa Jumuiya wa Windows Insider</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3871_232400_1389187"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to time when an individual has nothing scheduled and appears as  available.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232400">free</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1389187">huru</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38711_2255081_2257329"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any type of unwanted, unsolicited, telephone call. Common types of nuisance calls include prank calls, telemarketing calls, and silent calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255081">nuisance call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2257329">simu ya usumbufu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38712_2255107_2257330"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A keyboard layout in which the onscreen keyboard can be split into two halves, resulting into two halves of the keyboard towards the edge of the screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255107">split keyboard mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2257330">modi ya kugawanya kibodi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38713_2255108_2257399"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A keyboard layout in which the onscreen keyboard is attached to one edge of the window.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255108">docked mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2257399">modi ya pembeni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38714_2255109_2257327"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A keyboard layout in which the onscreen keyboard is centered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255109">centered mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2257327">modi ya katikati</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38715_2255110_2257328"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that shows multi-tap users how many times they need to tap a key to input a particular character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255110">Multi-tap guide</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2257328">Mwongozo wa midonoo anuwai</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38721_2255320_2257216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A catalog of information for apps, games, movies and TV shows based on dynamic information such as new or fastest rising, top free, best rated, and top paid.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2255320">chart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2257216">chati</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3873_231624_534163"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A logical entity that enables a server to communicate with an iSCSI device over an Internet Protocol (IP) network. Each iSCSI initiator can have one or more network adapters through which communication is established.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231624">iSCSI initiator</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534163">kianzilishi iSCSI</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38734_2258789_2260355"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The data from motion sensors which is processed to create information such as step counts or activities (such as walking, running).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2258789">motion data</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2260355">data ya mwendo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38736_2258791_2547073"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Playing or viewing activity that you can instantly see among people that you follow.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2258791">trending</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2547073">inayovuma</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38737_2258792_2547074"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To allow people to see your real name and Microsoft account picture.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2258792">trust</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2547074">aminifu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="38738_2258793_2547077"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To transfer content from an Xbox console to the Xbox service.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2258793">upload</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="254