e and benefit from projects by examining the risk-reward of each project, the available funds, the likelihood of a project's duration, and the expected outcomes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2394292">PPM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2554314">PPM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42317_2394292_2554316"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A formal approach used by organizations to orchestrate, prioritize and benefit from projects by examining the risk-reward of each project, the available funds, the likelihood of a project's duration, and the expected outcomes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2394292">PPM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2554316">usimamiaji wa jalada la kutia hati la kipangama</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="42326_2394553_2396428"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">After a build update, to load an app with domain data (such as data from a database, from the network, or from a file system), during the download process. Before this step, the app cannot be used.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2394553">hydrate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumbe