a are not attributed to an identified or identifiable natural person.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2839915">pseudonymisation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841865">upendeleo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50197_2839915_2841866"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The processing of personal data in such a manner that the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific data subject without the use of additional information, provided that such additional information is kept separately and is subject to technical and organisational measures to ensure that the personal data are not attributed to an identified or identifiable natural person.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2839915">pseudonymisation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841866">utambulisho</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50197_2839918_2841865"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The processing of personal data in such a manner that the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific data subject without the use of additional information, provided that such additional information is kept separately and is subject to technical and organisational measures to ensure that the personal data are not attributed to an identified or identifiable natural person.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2839918">pseudonymization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841865">upendeleo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50197_2839918_2841866"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The processing of personal data in such a manner that the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific data subject without the use of additional information, provided that such additional information is kept separately and is subject to technical and organisational measures to ensure that the personal data are not attributed to an identified or identifiable natural person.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2839918">pseudonymization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841866">utambulisho</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841643_2842267"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841643">call agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842267">wakala</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841643_2842273"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841643">call agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842273">wakala wa simu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841644_2842267"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841644">agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842267">wakala</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50216_2841644_2842273"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A person who handles a call to a business such as to fill service requests, place orders, or connect to another respondent or another call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841644">agent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842273">wakala wa simu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50217_2841650_2842298"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a call queue, a method of sending calls to agents whereby routing of incoming calls is balanced so that each call agent gets the same number of calls from the queue.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841650">round robin</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842298">simu zilizowianishwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50218_2841689_2842292"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A representation of the network requirements for connecting Microsoft Teams and cloud voice across an organization's physical locations using network details, teams usage, sites and Microsoft recommended personas (office workers, remote workers, and Teams room system).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841689">network plan</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842292">mpango wa mtandao</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50219_2841716_2842274"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of the Microsoft Teams Admin Center that shows detailed information about the devices, networks, and connectivity related to the calls and meetings for each user in a Microsoft Teams or Skype for Business tenant account. It is displayed on the user's Call History tab.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841716">Call Analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842274">Uchanganuzi wa Simu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50220_2841736_2842269"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information that gives insight into usage patterns and activity.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841736">analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842269">uchanganuzi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50221_2841755_2842271"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Microsoft teams, name of a tab on the Manage teams dialog that displays team analytics.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841755">Analytics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842271">Uchanganuzi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50222_2841766_2842272"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a call queue, a method of sending calls to agents whereby the first call in the queue rings all call agents at the same time. The first call agent to pick up the call gets the call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2841766">attendant routing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842272">uelekezaji wa mhudumu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Other</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50231_2842090_2845025"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To remove marked-up documents or data from a machine learning system and from the training process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842090">unseed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845025">ondoa data kwenye mfumo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50232_2842091_2844994"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To manipulate data intended to be parsed or otherwise processed by a software program in order to trigger hangs, exceptions, or crashes in the target application.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842091">fuzz</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844994">kufanya uluwihuwi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50233_2842092_2844997"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software program or tool that performs fuzz testing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842092">fuzzer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844997">fyuza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50234_2842093_2844995"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Invalid or random data used in fuzz testing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842093">fuzz</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844995">luwihuwi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842094_2844982"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842094">dial out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844982">piga ili kuwaalika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842094_2844989"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842094">dial out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844989">piga simu ya kuwaalika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842095_2844982"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842095">dial-out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844982">piga ili kuwaalika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50235_2842095_2844989"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">During an active meeting, to invite more people to join the meeting by dialing their phone number.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842095">dial-out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844989">piga simu ya kuwaalika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50236_2842096_2844980"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To join a conference call when the invited guest initiates the connection by phoning or by connecting through a computer with a conference ID or PIN. Contrast with dial out.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842096">dial in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844980">piga ili kujiunga</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50237_2842097_2844972"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A formula for finding any power of a binomial without multiplying at length. According to the theorem, it is possible to expand the polynomial (x + y)n into a polynomial sum expression.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842097">binomial theorem</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844972">usemi wa bainomi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50238_2842098_2844963"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A function that automatically changes passwords after a certain time interval.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842098">password rotation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844963">mzunguko wa nywila</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50239_2842099_2844959"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An account that provides access to Office 365.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842099">Office 365 account</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844959">Akaunti ya Office 365</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50240_2842100_2845020"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A PowerPoint feature that allows the user to enter rehearsal mode and while speaking receive on-screen guidance about pacing, inclusive language, use of filler words, and culturally insensitive phrases. At the end of each rehearsal session, a detailed report with metrics for additional practice is provided.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842100">Presenter Coach</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845020">Mkufunzi wa Mwasilishaji</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50241_2842101_2844985"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An optional feature of Skype for Business Server that allows meeting attendees to join the audio portion of a meeting by calling in to the meeting from a phone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842101">dial-in conferencing</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844985">mkutano wa kupiga ili kujiunga</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50242_2842102_2845006"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Microsoft Teams that lets users share their incoming calls with colleagues so that the colleagues can answer calls that occur while the user is unavailable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842102">group call pickup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845006">uchukuaji wa simu ya kikundi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50243_2842105_2844993"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Property of a private team that shows up in search results and is included in suggestions in the team gallery.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842105">discoverable</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844993">gundulika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50244_2842106_2844991"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of moving from physical to digital technologies in the workplace. An example is the adoption of cloud storage, which facilitates moving from physical offices to virtual ones.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842106">digital workspace transformation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844991">mgeuzo wa eneo la kazi la dijitali</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50245_2842107_2845004"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view in Microsoft Project that lists project information (tasks and milestones) in a table-like layout.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842107">Grid view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845004">Mwonekano wa gridi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50246_2842108_2844964"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view in Microsoft Project that shows the timeline of project activities and their dependencies.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842108">Timeline view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844964">Mwonekano wa kalenda ya matukio</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50247_2842109_2844956"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program for security software providers that gives them early access to vulnerability information so that they can provide updated protections to customers faster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842109">Microsoft Active Protections Program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844956">MAPP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50247_2842109_2845012"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program for security software providers that gives them early access to vulnerability information so that they can provide updated protections to customers faster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842109">Microsoft Active Protections Program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845012">Programu ya Ulinzi wa Microsoft Active</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50247_2842110_2844956"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program for security software providers that gives them early access to vulnerability information so that they can provide updated protections to customers faster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842110">MAPP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2844956">MAPP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50247_2842110_2845012"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program for security software providers that gives them early access to vulnerability information so that they can provide updated protections to customers faster.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842110">MAPP</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2845012">Programu ya Ulinzi wa Microsoft Active</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="50248_2842111_2844957"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A membership program that helps members get their products working and integrated with Windows by providing Windows APIs and other technologies including IOAV, AMSI and Cloud files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2842111">Microsoft Virus Initiative</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang