</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262429_1399280"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262429">Wi-Fi Protected Access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399280">Ufikivu Ulindwao wa Wi-Fi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262429_1399299"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262429">Wi-Fi Protected Access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399299">WPA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262430_1399280"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262430">WPA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399280">Ufikivu Ulindwao wa Wi-Fi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6317_262430_1399299"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A security method used by wireless networks. WPA encrypts the information that is sent between computers on a wireless network and authenticates users to help ensure that only authorized people can access the network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262430">WPA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399299">WPA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6319_343640_534814"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of managing business and/or social contacts in order to follow up, track conversations, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="343640">contact management</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534814">usimamizi wa wawasiliani</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6333_184278_2485999"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A BIOS developed to enable system-related information, such as information about hardware, to be gathered from computers on a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184278">SMBIOS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2485999">SMBIOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6333_184279_2485999"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A BIOS developed to enable system-related information, such as information about hardware, to be gathered from computers on a network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184279">system management BIOS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2485999">SMBIOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6349_345311_1399180"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of arranging data based on the order of specified information. For example, records sorted by class would list all records within a class before moving to records in the next class.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="345311">sorting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399180">upangaji</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6350_276560_534450"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The utility in Windows Vista that presents a view of all PCs, devices, and printers on the network, and is significantly faster and more reliable than My Network Places in Windows XP.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="276560">Network Explorer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534450">Kichunguzi Mtandao</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6352_152788_2772155"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method by which a client receives a stream, during which he/she cannot control the stream.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="152788">broadcast</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2772155">kutangaza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6374_58539_1389194"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A domain controller that holds a copy of the global catalog for the forest.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="58539">global catalog server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1389194">seva ya katologi nzima</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6378_7117_1796437"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An entry in either a securable object's discretionary access control list (DACL) or an object's system access control list (SACL). In a DACL, the entry grants or denies permissions to a user or group. In a SACL, the entry specifies which security events to audit for a particular user or group or controls the Windows Integrity Level for the object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7117">access control entry</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1796437">ACE</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6378_7119_1796437"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An entry in either a securable object's discretionary access control list (DACL) or an object's system access control list (SACL). In a DACL, the entry grants or denies permissions to a user or group. In a SACL, the entry specifies which security events to audit for a particular user or group or controls the Windows Integrity Level for the object.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7119">ACE</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1796437">ACE</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6381_141638_1396948"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control that, when clicked, expands or collapses a grouped record to display or hide its detail records.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141638">expand control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1396948">kidhibiti panuzi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6381_141638_1918640"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A control that, when clicked, expands or collapses a grouped record to display or hide its detail records.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141638">expand control</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1918640">kiashirio cha upanuzi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpe