 a specific page element, such as a headline or an important announcement.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="78424">marquee</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533506">kidoido</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6883_210434_1396902"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device used to copy files to recordable CDs and DVDs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210434">disc burner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1396902">kichoma CD</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6886_2911_532937"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A communications device that converts between digital data from a computer or terminal and analog audio signals that can pass through a standard telephone line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2911">modem</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="532937">modemu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</term