er's memory without using the computer's processor. DMA improves the performance of the device and frees the computer's processor so it can perform other tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="46146">direct memory access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1396910">DMA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7384_46147_1396898"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that allows certain devices, such as hard disks and CD or DVD drives, to transfer information directly through the computer's memory without using the computer's processor. DMA improves the performance of the device and frees the computer's processor so it can perform other tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="46147">DMA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1396898">ufikivu wa kumbukumbu moja kwa moja</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7384_46147_1396910"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that allows certain devices, such as hard disks and CD or DVD drives, to transfer information directly through the computer's memory without using the computer's processor. DMA improves the performance of the device and frees the computer's processor so it can perform other tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="46147">DMA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1396910">DMA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7389_217332_2118877"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A digital cellular phone technology (standard) first deployed in 1992. GSM uses narrowband TDMA, which allows eight simultaneous calls on the same radio frequency.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="217332">Global System for Mobile Communications</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118877">GSM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7389_217333_2118877"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A digital cellular phone technology (standard) first deployed in 1992. GSM uses narrowband TDMA, which allows eight simultaneous calls on the same radio frequency.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="217333">GSM</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2118877">GSM</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7395_46512_533275"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A notice that warns that the manufacturer of the product limits liability in certain situations/uses.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="46512">disclaimer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533275">ilani ya kujitoa hatiani</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7415_40207_1796455"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program that is used on a Web page to count the number of times that the Web page was accessed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="40207">counter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1796455">kihesabu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7416_73948_533468"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To align text along the left margin.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73948">left align</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="533468">pangilia kushoto</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7417_315143_534602"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A tag or string affixed to an item to provide identifying or descriptive information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="315143">label</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534602">lebo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7421_184828_534081"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To ask someone to engage in an instant conversation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184828">invite</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="534081">alika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7430_237835_1796480"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A shape on a stencil that you use repeatedly to create drawings.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237835">master</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1