ice that sends, or routes, information between two networks (for example, between a home network and the Internet).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="106258">router</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1399132">kipanga njia</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7933_265341_1165638"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Characterized by row or column-specific formatting. Often describes rows or columns of data that use alternating colors or shading to enhance readability.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="265341">banded</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1165638">- a safu maalumu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">KEN, TZA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7942_76244_1397078"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of rules and data specific to a language and a geographic area. Locales include information on sorting rules, date and time formatting, numeric and monetary conventions, and character classification.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="76244">locale</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="sw"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1397078">mand